  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Developing a Standardized Methodology for Camera Trap Monitoring of Amur Tigers in..Protected Areas in the Russian Far East</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this proposal is to replace the existing Amur tiger monitoring system in Russia based on tracks with a standardized methodology that relies on use of camera traps. The primary goal of this project is to implement this new system in all federally protected areas that hold important habitat for tigers in the Russian Far East. The secondary goal is to share this approach with appropriate entities in northeast China in an attempt to develop coordinated, trans-boundary survey protocols. This will be done by: 1) institutionalizing and expanding existing camera trap efforts to a total of six protected areas; 2) ensuring there is a standardized methodology used at all sites and obtaining governmental approval of the methodology; and 3) facilitating information sharing by developing a photographic database and beginning coordination of camera trap surveys and photographic databases with stakeholders in northeast China.</narrative>
  </description>
